  <h1>Delete Your Account</h1>
  <p class="updated">Last Updated: 22 July 2026</p>

  <p>You can permanently delete your Kroot account and associated data at any time, whether or not you currently have the app installed.</p>

  <h2>Option 1: Delete your account in the app</h2>
  <p>If you have Kroot installed, this is the fastest way:</p>
  <ol>
    <li>Open the Kroot app and sign in.</li>
    <li>Go to the <strong>Profile</strong> tab.</li>
    <li>Tap <strong>Delete Profile</strong>.</li>
    <li>Confirm the deletion when prompted.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>Your account is deleted immediately once you confirm &mdash; there is no waiting period.</p>

  <h2>Option 2: Request deletion without the app</h2>
  <div class="box">
    <p>If you no longer have the app installed, email us from the address associated with your Kroot account and we will delete your account and data on your behalf.</p>
    <p><a class="btn" href="mailto:admin@krootapp.com?subject=Account%20Deletion%20Request">Email admin@krootapp.com</a></p>
  </div>
  <p>Please include the phone number or email address you used to sign up so we can locate your account. We will confirm once your account has been deleted, typically within 7 business days.</p>

  <h2>What gets deleted</h2>
  <p>Deleting your account permanently removes your profile information (name, email, phone number, profile photo), the flashcards and decks you created, your study progress and badges, and your saved bank/payout details.</p>

  <h2>What we may retain</h2>
  <p>We may retain limited records where required for legal, tax, fraud-prevention, or accounting purposes &mdash; for example, records of completed payments or payouts. This information is kept only as long as necessary to meet those obligations and is not used for any other purpose.</p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>If you have any questions about this process, contact us at <a href="mailto:admin@krootapp.com">admin@krootapp.com</a>.</p>
